  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      58.56,
      503.29,
      529.89,
      574.27
    ],
    "text": "The low-pressure area that has formed over the Andaman Sea region of the Bay of Bengal is expected to intensify further over the next few days. Although this system will not have a direct impact on Sri Lanka, the prevailing rainy conditions in the southwestern part of the island are expected to continue due to the wind flow towards the system.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      5.039999961853027,
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      58.56,
      578.05,
      538.36,
      633.31
    ],
    "text": "Showers or thundershowers will occur at times in the Western, Sabaragamuwa and North-western provinces and in Galle, Matara, Kandy and Nuwara-Eliya Districts. Heavy falls about 100 mm are likely at some places in the above areas.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri",
      "Calibri,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      6.0,
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      58.56,
      636.22,
      463.97,
      654.31
    ],
    "text": "Several spells of showers may occur in North-central province and Mannar district.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      3.0,
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      58.56,
      657.61,
      538.32,
      693.7
    ],
    "text": "Showers or thundershowers will occur at several places in Uva province and in Batticaloa and Ampara districts after 2.00 p.m.",
    "fonts": [
